meta {
  name: Revert status
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/admins/users/:userId/requests/revert
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  userId: 1
}

body:json {
  {
    "current_status": 9,
    "target_status": 6,
    "delete_files": [
      "photo"
    ],
    "description": "แก้ไขข้อมูล"
  }
}

docs {
  Admin login (cookie Authentication_Admin): run "Admin auth / Login" first. `delete_files` (optional): any of `photo`, `govcard`, `expfile`. A Revert to 0 is only for a first-card request (Request Type 1); for a request of types 2-11 it is 400 "only a first-card request (Request Type 1) can be reverted to 0", so Revert it to 1, 6 or 7 instead. The new status entry carries the Request Type of the user's current request.
}
